{"kind":"request","text":"Passkeys for person-only acts, and key recovery practices (not urgent; after the current sequence unless reprioritized).\n\n1. A second key class for acts only people may take: approve, merge or promote, change the rules, invite, and release. Make the WebAuthn challenge the hash of the dap intent, and carry the assertion (authenticator data, client data JSON, signature) in the act's envelope. Membership enrolls a passkey public key to a person member. A guard can then require \"signed by a passkey enrolled to a person member\". Verification needs only the public key and the assertion, so dap verify and replay keep working offline, and an agent key can never satisfy that guard. This makes the MVP's people-only approval (notes/2026-10-16-repo-in-ai-mvp-plan.md) a native guarantee instead of a role-table convention: the \"an agent promotes itself\" case is refused by the room's rules. Use @simplewebauthn/server (or an equivalent small verifier) for verification only, as a reviewed dependency.\n2. Later, possibly: passkey sign-in and recovery for the browser page, with several passkeys and recovery codes. Keep it to reading sessions and enrolling keys, never to signing acts.\n3. Practices to adopt now, for device keys generally: several credentials from the start, and never removing the last one; a fresh check for anything that could lock the owner out (revoking keys, changing controllers); recovery codes stored only as hashes; one uniform refusal for any failed authentication. dap has little to say about recovering a lost device key today; these practices address that gap.\n\nReference implementation (read for design; BSD-2-Clause Plus Patent licence; do not copy code without attribution, and do not name it in repository notes): /Users/hughpyle/play/tmp/entries/open-integrity-forge, especially its WebAuthn challenge binding and its tests.\n\nDeliverables: a short preparation note in notes/implementation/ before Source (envelope form, guard form, membership enrollment and versioning, verify/replay path, which acts move to passkey-only, recovery practices), then Source in slices, and an implementation note in notes/implementation/ when built.","body":{"conditions":"Preparation note reviewed before Source; checker approves each exact head; gate passes once per head; an agent key cannot satisfy the person-passkey guard (witness), a person's passkey assertion bound to the exact intent hash is accepted, a replayed or re-targeted assertion is refused, and dap verify and replay check assertions offline; implementation note in notes/implementation/; push after landing; no Cloudflare deployment.","target":"inherit","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}